% Kind guarantees, exact comparison, counts, and server limits (T09).
%
% Scenario source: docs/interim/2026-09-29/worklist/tests/09-sql-kinds.md.
% The kind warrant (docs/internals/sql-kinds.md 1): SQL never reports a match for a
% row SEL would have refused. Expected strings are derived from that document and
% from the renderings already pinned in 19-kind-warrant.sqlt, 22-sargable-bindings.sqlt,
% 23-statements.sqlt and 27-slices.sqlt -- never copied from a host's output.
%
% Deliberately NOT pinned: literal width past DECIMAL(65) (PHP-C52, unreproduced),
% a compound SUM body over an UNKNOWN field (open, docs/internals/sql-kinds.md 5a),
% text-literal arithmetic and SQLite MIN/MAX storage classes (the oracle decides:
% sql/oracle/expressions.selo and rows.json).

### name: warrant.bool.if-cannot-launder-an-undeclared-column
--- note
The kind warrant (docs/internals/sql-kinds.md 1, 5): an operand nobody has vouched for is UNCERTAIN, and an uncertain operand in a boolean position is refused, on every dialect, because no dialect can ask "is this a boolean". A kind that becomes certain by passing THROUGH a conditional is the same hole: IF, COND, `??` and `???` yield UNKNOWN when any branch is UNKNOWN, whatever the other branches are. (JS-C27, PHP-C28)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
IF(TRUE, F, TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.if-cannot-launder-with-a-bool-condition
--- note
The condition being a certain BOOL changes nothing: the VALUE branches decide the kind of the result. (CPP-C29)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
IF(P, F, TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.coalesce-cannot-launder-an-undeclared-column
--- note
`??` is a conditional too. (JS-C27, PHP-C28)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
(F ?? TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.vacuous-coalesce-cannot-launder-an-undeclared-column
--- note
`???` likewise.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
(F ??? TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.cond-cannot-launder-an-undeclared-column
--- note
COND is the third conditional form.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
COND(P, F, TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.not-over-a-laundered-conditional
--- note
NOT reads its operand as a boolean too.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
NOT IF(TRUE, F, TRUE)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.if-cannot-launder-on-postgresql
--- note
Every dialect refuses; PostgreSQL would also fail at run time, which is not a reason to emit it.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
IF(TRUE, F, TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.coalesce-cannot-launder-on-sqlite
--- note
SQLite likewise.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
(F ?? TRUE) AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===

### name: warrant.bool.if-over-a-declared-bool-is-not-refused
--- note
CONTROL for the group above: declare the column BOOL and the promise transfers to the application, so the same program translates.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f", "type": "BOOL"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
IF(TRUE, F, TRUE) AND TRUE
--- expect
(CASE WHEN TRUE THEN `f` ELSE TRUE END AND TRUE)
===

### name: warrant.bool.coalesce-over-a-declared-bool-is-not-refused
--- note
CONTROL.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "f", "type": "BOOL"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}}
--- source
(F ?? TRUE) AND TRUE
--- expect
(COALESCE(`f`, TRUE) AND TRUE)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.coalesce-over-an-undeclared-column-is-guarded
--- note
An undeclared column in a numeric position is wrapped in the guard on a dialect that can ask "is this a number" and refused on one that cannot (docs/internals/sql-kinds.md 5). Passing through IF / COND / `??` / `COALESCE` does not make it certain: the conditional's kind is UNKNOWN when any value branch is, so the guard wraps the WHOLE conditional -- naming it twice, as every guard names its operand twice (warrant.raw.the-guard-evaluates-it-twice). Otherwise `'abc' + 1` is 1 on MariaDB where SEL raises E_NOT_NUM. (PHP-C28, LISP-C24)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
(U ?? 1) + 1 > 0
--- expect
((CASE WHEN (COALESCE(`u`, 1) REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(COALESCE(`u`, 1) AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END + 1) > 0)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.if-branch-unknown-is-guarded
--- note
An undeclared column in a numeric position is wrapped in the guard on a dialect that can ask "is this a number" and refused on one that cannot (docs/internals/sql-kinds.md 5). Passing through IF / COND / `??` / `COALESCE` does not make it certain: the conditional's kind is UNKNOWN when any value branch is, so the guard wraps the WHOLE conditional -- naming it twice, as every guard names its operand twice (warrant.raw.the-guard-evaluates-it-twice). Otherwise `'abc' + 1` is 1 on MariaDB where SEL raises E_NOT_NUM. (JS-C27, CPP-C29, LISP-C24)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(P, U, 1) + 1 == 2
--- expect
((CASE WHEN (CASE WHEN `p` THEN `u` ELSE 1 END REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(CASE WHEN `p` THEN `u` ELSE 1 END AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END + 1) = 2)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.coalesce-function-over-an-undeclared-column-is-guarded
--- note
The function spelling of `??`. (LISP-C24)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
COALESCE(U, 0) > 5
--- expect
(CASE WHEN (COALESCE(`u`, 0) REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(COALESCE(`u`, 0) AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END > 5)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.abs-over-a-laundered-conditional
--- note
A function argument that reads a number: the same wrap. (PHP-C28)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ABS(U ?? 1)
--- expect
ABS(CASE WHEN (COALESCE(`u`, 1) REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(COALESCE(`u`, 1) AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.min-over-a-laundered-conditional
--- note
(PHP-C28)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
MIN(U ?? 1, 2)
--- expect
LEAST(CASE WHEN (COALESCE(`u`, 1) REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(COALESCE(`u`, 1) AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END, 2)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.length-over-a-laundered-conditional
--- note
(PHP-C28)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
LEFT("abc", U ?? 1)
--- expect
LEFT('abc', CASE WHEN (COALESCE(`u`, 1) REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(COALESCE(`u`, 1) AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.an-undeclared-branch-on-the-right-is-guarded
--- note
Either side. (GO-C15)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
N < IF(TRUE, U, -1)
--- expect
(`n` < CASE WHEN (CASE WHEN TRUE THEN `u` ELSE (-1) END REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(CASE WHEN TRUE THEN `u` ELSE (-1) END AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.cond-branch-unknown-is-guarded
--- note
(GO-C15)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
COND(P, U, 1) + 1 == 2
--- expect
((CASE WHEN (CASE WHEN `p` THEN `u` ELSE 1 END REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(CASE WHEN `p` THEN `u` ELSE 1 END AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END + 1) = 2)
===

### name: warrant.numeric.sqlite-refuses-a-laundered-coalesce
--- note
SQLite cannot ask whether a value is a number, so a numeric position holding an UNCERTAIN operand is refused (warrant.numeric.sqlite-cannot-ask-and-refuses); a conditional does not make it certain. Measured against SQLite: `IF(FLAG,1,UNK) < 1` answered TRUE for unk='abc' where SEL raises E_NOT_NUM. (GO-C15)
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
(U ?? 1) + 1 > 0
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED
===

### name: warrant.numeric.sqlite-refuses-a-laundered-if-branch
--- note
SQLite cannot ask whether a value is a number, so a numeric position holding an UNCERTAIN operand is refused (warrant.numeric.sqlite-cannot-ask-and-refuses); a conditional does not make it certain. Measured against SQLite: `IF(FLAG,1,UNK) < 1` answered TRUE for unk='abc' where SEL raises E_NOT_NUM. (GO-C15)
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}, "P": {"kind": "column", "column": "p", "type": "BOOL"}, "N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(P, U, 1) + 1 == 2
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED
===

### name: warrant.numeric.sqlite-refuses-a-laundered-abs
--- note
SQLite cannot ask whether a value is a number, so a numeric position holding an UNCERTAIN operand is refused (warrant.numeric.sqlite-cannot-ask-and-refuses); a conditional does not make it certain. Measured against SQLite: `IF(FLAG,1,UNK) < 1` answered TRUE for unk='abc' where SEL raises E_NOT_NUM. (GO-C15)
--- dialect
sqlite
