### name: bind.in.exact.numeric-literal-item-is-cast
--- note
An `exact` column skips the byte cast on the column only because both sides are then text; a NUMBER item compared with bare `=` makes MariaDB compare numerically ('3.0' = 3 and '3abc' = 3 are TRUE), a match SEL refuses ('3.0' IN ("a", 3) is FALSE: EQL is structural). The item is cast the way `EQL` casts a number: S IN (1) is (`s` = CAST(1 AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin). (PY-C20, CPP-C30, LISP-C25)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "S": {"kind": "column", "column": "s", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
T IN ("a", 3)
--- expect
((`t` = 'a') OR (`t` = CAST(3 AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin))
===

### name: bind.in.exact.numeric-literal-items-only
--- note
(LISP-C25, CPP-C30)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "S": {"kind": "column", "column": "s", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
S IN (1, 2)
--- expect
((`s` = CAST(1 AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) OR (`s` = CAST(2 AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin))
===

### name: stmt.take.whole-number-with-scale.mariadb
--- note
SEL accepts a count written with a scale when its value is a whole number (`TAKE((1,2,3), 2.0)` is the first two): 2.0 is 2. The translator answered E_NOT_INT although the evaluator does not; a refusal in the safe direction, but a refusal SEL would not make (JS-C56, PHP-C50, CPP-C59).
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items"}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TAKE(2.0)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `items` LIMIT 2
===

### name: stmt.take.zero-with-scale.mariadb
--- note
`0.0` and `-0` are zero: TAKE gives nothing, as SEL does. (CPP-C59)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items"}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TAKE(0.0)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `items` LIMIT 0
===

### name: stmt.take.count-past-2^53.mariadb
--- note
A count is a decimal SEL number and is emitted exactly. JS routed it through a Number: 9007199254740993 became 9007199254740992 and 1e23 became `1e+23`. 2^53+1 and int64 max are inside every dialect's range. (JS-C55, GO-C38)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items"}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TAKE(9007199254740993)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `items` LIMIT 9007199254740993
===

