### name: stmt.take.count-past-int64-is-clamped.mariadb
--- note
SEL has no limit and a TAKE count past the end of any list is the whole list; the servers accept at most 2^63-1 (PostgreSQL, SQLite) or 2^64-1 (MariaDB, MySQL). The rendered count is clamped to 9223372036854775807 on every dialect -- a value all four accept -- so 1e23 is never emitted (LIMIT 99999999999999999999999 is rejected by PostgreSQL and SQLite). Verified on the servers by tools/check-sql-limits.php. (PY-C41, LISP-C39, GO-C38, JS-C55, CPP-C59)
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items"}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TAKE(99999999999999999999999)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `items` LIMIT 9223372036854775807
===

### name: stmt.take.count-2^63-is-clamped.mariadb
--- note
The first count past int64 max.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
