### name: stmt.drop.merged-offset-past-int64-is-clamped.mariadb
--- note
The clamp is applied to the MERGED count: DROP(a) .> DROP(b) is the offset a+b (`ITEMS .> DROP(2) .> DROP(1)` is OFFSET 3), and 9223372036854775807 + 1 is clamped, not wrapped, refused or nested.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items"}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> DROP(9223372036854775807) .> DROP(1)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `items` LIMIT 18446744073709551615 OFFSET 9223372036854775807
===

