### name: stmt.take.negative-fraction.mariadb
--- note
A negative count that is not whole is E_NOT_INT, as SEL raises it (the integer check before the sign): the PHP translator tested the sign first and answered E_RANGE.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "items", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TAKE(-1.5)
--- error
E_NOT_INT 1:15
===

### name: stmt.drop.negative-fraction.mariadb
--- note
A negative count that is not whole is E_NOT_INT, as SEL raises it (the integer check before the sign): the PHP translator tested the sign first and answered E_RANGE.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "items", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> DROP(-0.5)
--- error
E_NOT_INT 1:15
===

### name: stmt.top-by.negative-fraction.mariadb
--- note
A negative count that is not whole is E_NOT_INT, as SEL raises it (the integer check before the sign): the PHP translator tested the sign first and answered E_RANGE.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "items", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> TOP_BY(_["id"], -2.5)
--- error
E_NOT_INT 1:26
===
